                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_08\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes KVMPhysicalDisk.java's rbd option string construction from:\n    rbdOpts += \"\\\\\\\\:\" + monPort;\nto:\n    rbdOpts += \"\\\\:\" + monPort;\ni.e. it removes an extra level of backslash escaping applied when building the \"mon_host=<host>\\:<port>\" segment of the rbd connection string, because the host/port separator was being double-escaped.\n\ncandidate_08 is the commit that originally introduces the RBDStringBuilder() static method (in agent/src/com/cloud/agent/storage/KVMPhysicalDisk.java, as part of adding RBD/Ceph storage support to the KVM plugin). The very first version of this method contains the line:\n\n    rbdOpts += \":mon_host=\" + monHost + \"\\\\\\\\:\" + monPort;\n\nThis is exactly the double-escaped pattern later corrected by the fix commit. Searching all 20 candidates for occurrences of \"mon_host\"/\"RBDStringBuilder\"/\"rbdOpts\" shows candidate_08 is the earliest (and only originating) commit containing this code \u2014 candidates 09 and earlier (01-07, 09, 10) do not touch this code at all, confirming it did not exist before candidate_08. Later candidates (11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 19, 20) merely carry the code forward through package refactors (moving it into plugins/hypervisors/kvm/...) and unrelated logic changes (e.g., candidate_12 adds a `monPort != 6789` condition around the same buggy `\"\\\\\\\\:\"` string, but does not fix the escaping itself), while still retaining the double-escaped separator until the actual fix commit.\n\nTherefore candidate_08 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
